# Valve's deckard (Steam Frame) gamescope, rebuilt with Kettle Linux's patches.
# Replaces deckard's gamescope 3.16.30-1, built from Valve's 3.16.30 tag (ad2763da): the same
# commit of Valve's public repo is built here, so nothing but the patches differs.
#
# Snapdragon Game Super Resolution 1 (the sgsr filter, value 5 = what Steam Frame's "Sharp"
#   writes: SGSR 1 upscale (Qualcomm, BSD-3-Clause, notice in src/shaders/sgsr1.h) then RCAS),
#   the scaling_filter/scaling_sharpness gamescopectl commands, RCAS at one pixel per thread on
#   Adreno, composite_timing and the mangoapp filter report are Valve's own since 3.16.29; our
#   0001-0008 cherry-picked them onto 3.16.28 and are gone.
# 0009 (ours) adds the steam_sharp_filter convar: which filter Steam's Sharp runs
#   (default sgsr; `gamescopectl steam_sharp_filter fsr` gives FSR 1 back).
# 0010 (ours) reports mapped xdg-shell windows to Steam as focusable (app IDs, and windows
#   under a synthetic id), so native Wayland games (Lepton's Android window) come to the front.
# 0011 (ours) GAMESCOPE_INTERNAL_PHYSICAL_SIZE=WxH (mm) overrides the size clients see for the
#   built-in panel, which Steam picks its UI scale from (the Thor's panel driver reports one
#   that made Game Mode's UI too large for the screen).
# 0012-0016 let a second screen run alongside Game Mode (the Thor's bottom panel): gamescope
#   leases that connector (--lease-connector) and hands the lease over a Unix socket to a second
#   gamescope (--drm-lease-client), forwarding it the panel's touchscreen (--ignore-touch-device).
#   0012 and 0013 are OpenGamingCollective's PRs #13 (squashed, without its HDR change) and #20;
#   0014-0016 are Armada's 0013-0015, ported without the drm-lease-v1 protocol they sit on
#   (which only apps that request a lease themselves, e.g. emulators, need). BSD-2-Clause,
#   as gamescope.
# 0017 (ours) keeps the second screen's gamescope from sending mangoapp its frames: every
#   gamescope uses the same message queue, and Game Mode's MangoHud flickered between the two.
# 0018 (ours) counts the second screen's touches as input, which Steam's idle dimming and sleep
#   go by: touching the bottom screen didn't bring back a dimmed top one.
# 0019 (ours) gives an internal panel without an EDID (DSI) its native modes as refresh rates:
#   gamescope listed none for the Portal's 60/120 Hz panel, so it could never leave 120 Hz.
# (0020, ours until 20261006: a frame limit at the lowest refresh rate it divides. Dropped: Steam's
#   frame limit slider labels each stop with the highest such rate, so the panel now runs at that.)
# 0021 (ours) adds ui_refresh_hz (env gamescope_ui_refresh_hz): the refresh rate while no game is
#   open, for a lower-power Steam UI; 0 (default) keeps the display's highest.
# 0022 (ours) adds GAMESCOPE_GENERATED_REFRESH_RATES: lower rates an EDID-less panel doesn't list,
#   made at a lower pixel clock; the Thor's bottom screen offers 30 Hz with it (Quick Access >
#   Screens).
# 0023 (ours) adds refresh_hz (env gamescope_refresh_hz): a fixed refresh rate whatever Steam asks
#   for, which Quick Access > Power sets; 0 (its Auto) lets Steam's frame limit pick the rate.
# 0024 (ours) adds auto_refresh_max_hz (env gamescope_auto_refresh_max_hz): with no frame limit, or
#   no game focused, the highest rate at or below it; frame limits still pick any rate. The Portal
#   sets 120: Auto runs uncapped at 120 Hz, but a 55 fps limit at 165 and 145 fps at 145.
#
# To follow a newer deckard gamescope, move _commit to the one its `gamescopectl version`
# names and drop whichever patches it already contains.
pkgname=gamescope
pkgver=3.16.30
pkgrel=1.1
_commit=ad2763da1c48860f649abfe842a087188dcb6e20
pkgdesc='gaming shell based on Xwayland, powered by Vulkan and DRM (deckard + Kettle Linux, SGSR 1)'
arch=(aarch64)
url='https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope'
license=(BSD-2-Clause MIT BSD-3-Clause)
# deckard's list; the binary also links SDL2, lcms2, libxkbcommon, libX* that these pull in
depends=(xorg-xwayland libavif aom rav1e libxres xcb-util-errors freerdp xcb-util-wm
         libxcomposite pixman libinput seatd pipewire libxmu libxcursor libdecor libei luajit
         libdrm)
makedepends=(git meson cmake ninja glslang vulkan-headers wayland-protocols
             sdl2 vulkan-icd-loader lcms2 libxtst hwdata)
install=gamescope.install
source=("git+https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope.git#commit=$_commit"
        "git+https://github.com/Joshua-Ashton/GamescopeShaders.git#tag=v0.1"
        steamos-session-shell
        0009-steamcompmgr-let-steam_sharp_filter-pick-what-Steam-.patch
        0010-steamcompmgr-report-mapped-xdg-shell-windows-to-Stea.patch
        0011-drm-GAMESCOPE_INTERNAL_PHYSICAL_SIZE-overrides-the-in.patch
        0012-DRM-lease-a-connector-to-a-companion-app-over-a-Unix.patch
        0013-DRM-detach-conflicting-pipelines-before-creating-the.patch
        0014-DRM-run-a-compositor-from-the-leased-output-drm-leas.patch
        0015-wlserver-always-swallow-the-ignored-touch-device.patch
        0016-DRM-blank-the-leased-connector-when-the-companion-go.patch
        0017-mangoapp-a-drm-lease-client-gamescope-sends-mangoapp.patch
        0018-wlserver-touches-passed-to-a-lease-companion-still-c.patch
        0019-DRM-offer-an-EDID-less-internal-panel-s-native-modes-.patch
        0021-steamcompmgr-add-ui_refresh_hz-the-refresh-rate-while-n.patch
        0022-DRM-offer-generated-lower-refresh-rates-for-an-EDID-.patch
        0023-steamcompmgr-add-refresh_hz-a-fixed-refresh-rate.patch
        0024-steamcompmgr-add-auto_refresh_max_hz-a-ceiling-while.patch)
sha256sums=('SKIP'
            'SKIP'
            'a34b30f8c58881f29a632ae1b4c8d7fbd7ba8c1ae6509d2b85afe362cad6de93'
